From 60d302b2d3e92b57340f4aa12fb6ab8c8016c095 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlitokenn <Charlitokenn@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 07:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web shell: don't show "Not connected" for a tenant that's
 still provisioning

WebShell.vue's unavailable screen showed the alarming "Not connected"
title for any non-READY tenant status, including PROJECT_CREATED - a
legitimate, recoverable in-between state where the Neon project exists
but the schema migration hasn't completed (or is waiting on the manual
'npm run migrate:tenants -- --include-project-created' recovery run,
see custom/web/db/tenantMigrationRunner.ts).

- Extract the boot-status -> shell-state mapping out of src/web/shell.ts
  into a pure src/web/shellBootState.ts, testable without a live Clerk
  session.
- Add a stillProvisioning flag to the ShellState 'unavailable' variant
  and give PROJECT_CREATED its own copy instead of the generic 'account
  not ready yet' text.
- WebShell.vue shows 'Setting up your account' instead of 'Not
  connected' when stillProvisioning is set; genuine failures
  (FAILED/SUSPENDED/UNKNOWN) are unchanged.
- Widen WebFyoStatus to include SUSPENDED, which the control plane can
  legitimately return here but the type didn't account for.
- Add tests/shellBootState.spec.ts covering all five statuses.
